course: dictionary
lesson: 10865
title: Victim
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A victim is a person, or sometimes an animal, who is hurt, harmed or tricked by someone or something else. «A burglary is when someone breaks into a home to steal; victims are often upset most by feeling unsafe.» The victim did not cause the harm.
explain: Victim is a noun, and its plural is victims. You will see it in phrases like «a victim of a crime», «fall victim to» a scam, and «flood victims», who were harmed by a flood. Careful: «play the victim» means pretending to be treated badly when you are not.
explain: The most important idea is that it is never the victim's fault. «Bystanders can help stop bullying by not joining in, supporting the victim and telling an adult.» If something bad happens to you, tell a trusted adult.
fact: A victim is a person or animal that is hurt, killed or harmed by someone else, an accident or an illness.
fact: Someone who is tricked or cheated is also a victim, for example a victim of a scam.
fact: You can be a victim of something you did not choose, such as a flood.
fact: It is never the victim's fault.
fact: If you are a victim of bullying, tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «Bystanders can help stop bullying by not joining in, supporting the victim and telling an adult.» Who is the victim in this sentence? | The bystanders | *The person being bullied | The adult who is told | The person who joins in
exercise: Ella says a victim of a scam is someone who wins a prize. What is a victim of a scam? | *Someone who has been tricked or cheated | Someone who helps stop scams | Someone who writes scams for a living | Someone who has won money in a game
exercise: What does «flood victims» mean? | *People harmed by a flood, through no fault of their own | People who cause floods | People who build bridges over water | People who swim in rivers for fun
test: «A burglary is when someone breaks into a home to steal; victims are often upset most by feeling unsafe.» What are victims often upset most by? | Losing their favourite socks | *Feeling unsafe | Having a sunny day | Eating dinner late
test: If someone is being bullied, what should they do? | Hide the problem and say nothing ever | *Tell a trusted adult | Think it is their own fault | Join in with the bullies
exam: Which statement about a victim is true? | *It is never the victim's fault | It is always the victim's fault | Victims cause their own bad luck every time | Victims are always to blame for scams
